  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "text": "The eruption broke the cable, cutting Tonga off until repairs.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "International Telecommunication Union",
      "role": "consequence"
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "text": "The cable lands on shore and links the islands to the global network; repairs need a specialist ship.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "VERIFIED FACT",
      "source": "International Telecommunication Union",
      "role": "mechanism"
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "text": "The key figure: 37 km.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "International Telecommunication Union",
      "role": "number"
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "text": "Why 1 broken cable cut off Tonga.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C5",
      "text": "In 2022, Hunga Tonga's plume rose 58 kilometres.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "text": "It broke Tonga's international cable 37 kilometres offshore.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C7",
      "text": "A domestic cable broke 47 kilometres out as well.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C8",
      "text": "That single cable was Tonga's link to Fiji and the world.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C9",
      "text": "Repairs had to wait for a specialist ship.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C10",
      "text": "That's why one cable landing is never enough.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C11",
      "text": "Southern Cross Cable reported that the eruption may have broken the Tonga Cable System, which connects Tonga to Southern Cross's trans-Pacific cable in Fiji.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "VERIFIED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — 2022 Hunga Tonga–Hunga Haʻapai eruption and tsunami",
      "role": "evidence",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Hunga_Tonga–Hunga_Haʻapai_eruption_and_tsunami"
    },
    {
      "id": "C12",
      "text": "Southern Cross cited a fault in the international cable 37 km (23 mi) from Nukuʻalofa, and a further fault in a domestic cable 47 km (29 mi) from Nukuʻalofa.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "VERIFIED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — 2022 Hunga Tonga–Hunga Haʻapai eruption and tsunami",
      "role": "evidence",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Hunga_Tonga–Hunga_Haʻapai_eruption_and_tsunami"
    },
    {
      "id": "C13",
      "text": "A large eruption commenced on 14 January 2022 at 04:20 local time, sending clouds of ash 20 km into the atmosphere.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "VERIFIED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — 2022 Hunga Tonga–Hunga Haʻapai eruption and tsunami",
      "role": "evidence",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Hunga_Tonga–Hunga_Haʻapai_eruption_and_tsunami"
    },
    {
      "id": "C14",
      "text": "The eruption column from this eruption rose 58 km (36 mi) into the mesosphere.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "VERIFIED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — 2022 Hunga Tonga–Hunga Haʻapai eruption and tsunami",
      "role": "evidence",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Hunga_Tonga–Hunga_Haʻapai_eruption_and_tsunami"
    },
    {
      "id": "C15",
      "text": "Reuters reported that a specialist cable repair ship would arrive at the Tongan archipelago on 30 January.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "VERIFIED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — 2022 Hunga Tonga–Hunga Haʻapai eruption and tsunami",
      "role": "evidence",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Hunga_Tonga–Hunga_Haʻapai_eruption_and_tsunami"
    },
    {
      "id": "C16",
      "text": "Tonga's international internet depended on a single submarine cable to Fiji.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "VERIFIED FACT",
      "source": "International Telecommunication Union",
      "role": "dependency"
    },
    {
      "id": "C17",
      "text": "With only one international cable, there was no alternative path.",
      "class": "MODEL",
      "layer": "MODEL",
      "source": "International Telecommunication Union",
      "role": "bottleneck"
    },
    {
      "id": "C18",
      "text": "Satellite links restored limited service in the meantime.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "VERIFIED FACT",
      "source": "International Telecommunication Union",
      "role": "resilience"
    },
    {
      "id": "C19",
      "text": "A cable landing point is the location where a submarine or other underwater cable makes landfall.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "consequence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Lead",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C20",
      "text": "The term is most often used for the landfall points of submarine telecommunications cables and submarine power cables.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "event",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Lead",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C21",
      "text": "The landing will either be direct (in the case of a point-to-point cable system) or via a branch from a main cable using a submarine branching unit.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "event",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Lead",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C22",
      "text": "The branch can be several kilometres long.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "event",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Lead",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C23",
      "text": "Such locations are rare, and will usually be the shared landfall point for several cable systems.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Selection criteria",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C24",
      "text": "Frequently, there will be a nearby cable landing station, or cable termination station, which may well be shared between multiple cable systems, but in some cases, the cable may be laid many miles inland before reaching its termination point.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C25",
      "text": "A cable landing station may or may not be required, depending on whether, for example, the submarine cable requires power in order to provide power to submarine repeaters or amplifiers.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C26",
      "text": "The voltages applied to the cables can be high—3,000 to 4,000 volts for a typical trans-Atlantic telecommunications cable system, and 1,000 volts for a cross-channel telecommunications cable system.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C27",
      "text": "Submarine power cables can operate at many kilovolts: for example, the Fenno-Skan power cable operates at 400 kV DC A cable termination station is the point at which the submarine cable connects into the land-based infrastructure or network.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C28",
      "text": "A cable termination station may be the same facility as the cable landing station, or may be many miles away.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C29",
      "text": "The termination station will usually be the point where high-capacity 'backhaul' land-based network connects to areas of high demand, which are usually centres of high population density, rather than the usually remote locations of cable landing points/landing stations/termination stations.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C30",
      "text": "A good example of this is the Endeavour cable system which connects Australia to Hawaii.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C31",
      "text": "The cable landing point in Sydney is Tamarama Beach, four kilometres from the cable termination station in Paddington.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C32",
      "text": "For power cables the term cable termination station is not strictly determined.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C33",
      "text": "It is either the point where the underwater cable ends and where the overhead powerline starts or if the whole line is implemented as cable, the first cable sleeve on the land.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C34",
      "text": "The substation or HVDC static inverter plant where the connection to the grid is established can also be described as a cable termination station; however, this station may be located far from the coast.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable landing point",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_landing_point",
      "section": "Associated facilities",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    }
